dictions, plus Politically Exposed Person (PEP) data. Downloadable in bulk and searchable via API.","howTo":["Search by name for instant results","Download the full dataset for bulk screening: available in CSV, JSON, and Excel","Use the API for automated checks: api.opensanctions.org","Cross-reference with OpenCorporates for corporate structure context"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free","api"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["dataset","finance"],"agentTool":"osint.opensanctions"},{"id":"kaggle","name":"Kaggle","url":"https://www.kaggle.com/search?q=","hostname":"kaggle.com","summary":"Largest community platform for datasets and data science notebooks.","detail":"Hosts 50,000+ public datasets across all topics. Many OSINT-relevant datasets exist: social media data, breach data, geolocation data, and more. Also has Jupyter notebook examples for analysis.","howTo":["Search for your topic","Filter by dataset type and size","Preview data in the browser before downloading","Fork existing notebooks for ready-to-run analysis code"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["dataset"],"agentTool":"osint.kaggle"},{"id":"github-code-search","name":"GitHub Code Search","url":"https://github.com/search","hostname":"github.com","summary":"Search all public GitHub repos for code, files, and commits.","detail":"GitHub's powerful code search. Search across billions of files in public repositories. Find API keys, credentials, internal hostnames, and other sensitive data accidentally committed to public repos.","howTo":["Use the Code search tab","Search: org:targetcompany password or org:targetcompany apikey","Filter by language, repo, and date","Check commit history for deleted content that may still be in git history"],"proTip":"Use: path:.env to find .env files. path:config OR path:settings combined with a company name often surfaces credentials.","alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["source_codes"],"agentTool":"osint.github-code-search"},{"id":"grep-app","name":"Grep.app","url":"https://grep.app","hostname":"grep.app","summary":"Fast regex search across 500,000 GitHub repositories.","detail":"Faster and more regex-capable than GitHub's native search. Searches across 500,000 public repos. Use regular expressions to find patterns like API keys, connection strings, and email addresses in code.","howTo":["Enter a keyword or regex pattern","Filter by language or repository","Use regex: [A-Za-z0-9]{32} matches many API key formats","Review matching files and surrounding context"],"proTip":"Combine with company name: search 'COMPANY_NAME' with regex for key patterns to find employee-committed secrets.","alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["source_codes"],"agentTool":"osint.grep-app"},{"id":"publicwww","name":"PublicWWW","url":"https://publicwww.com","hostname":"publicwww.com","summary":"Search the source code of 8 billion web pages.","detail":"Searches the HTML source code of 8 billion indexed web pages. Find which websites use a specific piece of code, tracking pixel, analytics ID, or technology. Excellent for linking sites that share infrastructure.","howTo":["Enter a code snippet, Google Analytics ID, or other unique identifier","Review sites sharing that code","Google Analytics IDs (UA-XXXXXXXX-X) link sites owned by the same person","Facebook Pixel IDs and AdSense publisher IDs work the same way"],"proTip":"Find all sites owned by a target by searching for their Google Analytics or AdSense ID in the source code.","alternatives":[],"tags":["web","freemium"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["source_codes"],"agentTool":"osint.publicwww"},{"id":"pastes-search-engine-cse","name":"Pastes Search Engine (CSE)","url":"https://cse.google.com/cse?cx=661713d0371832a02","hostname":"cse.google.com","summary":"Google Custom Search for paste sites \u2014 finds sensitive data in pastes.","detail":"Custom search engine scoped to Pastebin, GitHub Gist, Ghostbin, and other paste sites. Useful for finding leaked credentials, API keys, and internal documents shared on paste services.","howTo":["Enter email addresses, domain names, or other identifiers","Review paste results","Click through to read the full paste","Note the paste date for timeline analysis"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["source_codes"],"agentTool":"osint.pastes-search-engine-cse"},{"id":"shhgit","name":"Shhgit","url":"https://github.com/eth0izzle/shhgit","hostname":"github.com","summary":"Real-time GitHub secret detection \u2014 monitors new commits for credentials.","detail":"Monitors the GitHub event stream in real-time and alerts when new commits contain secrets matching 120+ patterns: AWS keys, Slack tokens, private keys, passwords, and more.","howTo":["Install: go install github.com/eth0izzle/shhgit@latest","Run: shhgit","Configure custom patterns in config.yaml","Monitor the output stream for matching commits"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["cli","free"],"installCommand":"go install github.com/eth0izzle/shhgit@latest","categoryIds":["source_codes"],"agentTool":"osint.shhgit"},{"id":"who-is","name":"Who.is","url":"https://who.is","hostname":"who.is","summary":"Clean WHOIS lookup with historical data and reverse search.","detail":"WHOIS lookup service with a focus on data presentation and historical records. Shows current and past registration data, IP information, and DNS records in a clean interface.","howTo":["Enter a domain name or IP address","Review current registrant info (often redacted post-GDPR)","Check the History tab for past WHOIS records before privacy was applied","Use registrant email or phone for reverse WHOIS lookups"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["whois"],"agentTool":"osint.who-is"},{"id":"whoxy","name":"Whoxy","url":"https://www.whoxy.com","hostname":"whoxy.com","summary":"Reverse WHOIS \u2014 find all domains registered by the same email or name.","detail":"Reverse WHOIS database. Enter an email address, registrant name, or phone number to find all domains registered by that entity. Extremely powerful for mapping an organization's or individual's domain portfolio.","howTo":["Select Reverse WHOIS from the top menu","Enter the registrant email, name, or phone","Review all domains registered by that entity","Follow any new domains found through standard WHOIS for additional leads"],"proTip":"Many registrants use the same email for all their domains. One leaked email can reveal an entire network of sites.","alternatives":[],"tags":["web","freemium"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["whois"],"agentTool":"osint.whoxy"},{"id":"whois-history-osint-sh","name":"WHOIS History (OSINT.SH)","url":"https://osint.sh/whoishistory","hostname":"osint.sh","summary":"Historical WHOIS records \u2014 see who registered a domain before privacy protection.","detail":"Shows historical WHOIS records for a domain. Many domains have old records from before GDPR/CCPA-driven privacy protection was applied. These historical records often contain real registrant names, addresses, and emails.","howTo":["Enter the domain name","Review the timeline of WHOIS records","Look for records predating 2018 when privacy protection became widespread","Note any real names or emails from early records"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["whois"],"agentTool":"osint.whois-history-osint-sh"},{"id":"shodan","name":"Shodan","url":"https://shodan.io","hostname":"shodan.io","summary":"Search engine for internet-connected devices and exposed services.","detail":"Shodan crawls the entire internet and indexes banners from every open port. Find exposed servers, webcams, industrial control systems, and databases. Use filters to narrow by country, organization, port, and product.","howTo":["Search by IP, hostname, or keyword (e.g., 'apache')","Use filters: hostname:target.com, org:'Company Name', port:8080, country:US","Click any result for full banner and history","Use the Explore page to browse interesting exposed systems"],"proTip":"Shodan API query: api.shodan.io/shodan/host/IP?key=APIKEY \u2014 great for automated enrichment.","alternatives":[],"tags":["web","api","freemium"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["domain_ip_dns"],"agentTool":"osint.shodan"},{"id":"securitytrails","name":"SecurityTrails","url":"https://securitytrails.com","hostname":"securitytrails.com","summary":"Historical DNS records, subdomains, and associated infrastructure.","detail":"Comprehensive DNS intelligence platform. View current and historical DNS records, subdomain lists, and associated IP addresses. The history feature is invaluable for finding infrastructure before it was moved or hidden.","howTo":["Enter a domain name","Review current DNS records (A, MX, NS, TXT)","Click 'History' for each record type to see past values","Check 'Subdomains' tab for a full list","Use associated IPs to find other domains on the same infrastructure"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","freemium"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["domain_ip_dns"],"agentTool":"osint.securitytrails"},{"id":"crt-sh","name":"CRT.sh","url":"https://crt.sh","hostname":"crt.sh","summary":"Certificate Transparency log search \u2014 surfaces all SSL certificates for a domain.","detail":"Every SSL/TLS certificate issued by a trusted CA is logged in public Certificate Transparency logs. Searching these logs reveals all subdomains that have ever had a certificate issued \u2014 even if the DNS has been removed.","howTo":["Enter %.domain.com (with % wildcard) to find all subdomains","Review certificate subject/SAN fields for subdomain enumeration","Sort by issuance date to find recently added subdomains","Look for internal-sounding names that shouldn't be public"],"proTip":"The SQL interface (crt.sh/?q=%.domain.com&output=json) returns JSON for programmatic processing.","alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["domain_ip_dns"],"agentTool":"osint.crt-sh"},{"id":"dnsdumpster","name":"DNSDumpster","url":"https://dnsdumpster.com","hostname":"dnsdumpster.com","summary":"DNS recon \u2014 maps subdomains, MX records, and hosting providers.","detail":"Free DNS reconnaissance tool that finds subdomains, MX records, TXT records, and generates a visual map of the DNS infrastructure. Also identifies hosting providers and geographic locations.","howTo":["Enter the target domain","Review the discovered subdomains and records","Download the visual infrastructure map (PNG)","MX records reveal the email provider; NS records reveal the DNS provider and registrar"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["domain_ip_dns"],"agentTool":"osint.dnsdumpster"},{"id":"urlscan-io","name":"URLScan.io","url":"https://urlscan.io","hostname":"urlscan.io","summary":"Scans URLs and captures screenshot, DOM, network requests, and indicators.","detail":"Submit a URL and URLScan renders it in a sandboxed browser, capturing a screenshot, DOM content, HTTP requests, cookies, and JavaScript variables. View without visiting the site yourself.","howTo":["Paste the target URL","Click Scan (Public scan is shared \u2014 use Unlisted for sensitive URLs)","Review the screenshot to see what the page looks like","Check the 'Network' tab for all resources loaded (APIs, CDNs, trackers)","Indicators tab shows IPs, domains, and certificates for pivoting"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["domain_ip_dns"],"agentTool":"osint.urlscan-io"},{"id":"viewdns-info","name":"ViewDNS.info","url":"https://viewdns.info","hostname":"viewdns.info","summary":"20+ DNS tools \u2014 reverse IP, whois, traceroute, port scan, and more.","detail":"A collection of 20+ DNS and network intelligence tools in one int